  "loc.messages.ServiceConnectionCredentialsUnavailable": "The '%s' service connection does not carry credentials that sqlcmd can use. The deployment was stopped rather than continued, because without them sqlcmd authenticates with whatever ambient identity the agent provides - a managed identity, an Azure CLI session or AZURE_* environment variables - instead of the service connection you selected.",
  "loc.messages.IntegratedAuthNotImplementedBySqlcmd": "sqlcmd does not implement Active Directory Integrated authentication and falls back to Active Directory Default, so the script may run under a different identity than the signed-in domain account. Use Active Directory Service Principal or Active Directory Managed Identity to state the identity explicitly.",
  "loc.messages.FirewallManagementRequiresAzureSqlDatabase": "Firewall rule management is only supported for Azure SQL Database, and '%s' is not an Azure SQL Database logical server. Managed instances, Fabric SQL and SQL Server on a virtual machine or on premises do not have Azure SQL firewall rules. Set firewallRuleManagement to false and allow the agent through the network yourself.",
  "loc.messages.ClientHasAccessToServer": "Client has access to SQL server. Skip adding firewall exception.",
